# Force LF line endings for everything text-based, regardless of the
# committer's platform. Without this, a shell script edited/committed on
# Windows can pick up CRLF, and bash on the Pi will fail with:
#   -bash: ./install.sh: /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
# which looks like a missing interpreter but is actually a stray \r in the
# shebang line. See setup/README.md "Workflow" section.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
*.cfg.in text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
